WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.890
What have we got next?

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.120
English. And we've got a quiz.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.440
What? Seriously?

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.860
Nishina, did you study?

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.830
You know me. I <i>obviously</i> totally did...

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:13.900
...absolutely nothing for it.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.460
As if I could study after practice.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.080
Huh?

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.220
What's wrong?

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.360
Oh, nothing!

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.960
Nothing at all!

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:36.010
I wanna speak to ya

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:36.010
before practice after school

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:36.010
Meet me in the

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:36.010
inner courtyard

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:36.010
Anita

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.010
<i>"I wanna speak to ya before
practice after school."</i>

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.540
<i>"Meet me in the inner courtyard."</i>

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:12.570
<b>Lock On!</b>

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.910
<i>Why would Anita want to talk to me?</i>

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.570
<i>Don't tell me she's....</i>

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.260
I've always had a thing for you!

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.990
<i>Oh boy, that'll cause issues for the team.</i>

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.510
Oh, he's here.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.450
Sorry for callin' ya out here.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:27.440
What's going on?

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.420
What's she doing here?

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.670
Oh, I get it.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.760
Girls get embarrassed about this stuff.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.640
But you know, we're only 
first-years in middle school.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.880
And you gotta think how it'd affect the team...

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:43.220
Then again, I don't hate that you're into me.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:46.740
Huh? What the heck are ya babblin' 'bout?

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.110
As if there's anythin' 'bout <i>you</i>
I'd fall in love with.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:49.560
Huh?

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.990
But there <i>is</i> a girl with weird taste
who totally digs ya.

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:54.520
What?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:59.490
It looks like my older sister 
is pretty interested in you.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.700
A-Are you serious?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.570
But what's that got to do with anything?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:07.660
We're still short on players.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:12.170
Meanin' that mushroom ya recruited
spits on us, knowin' we can't do jack.

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:15.500
The captain won't chew him out 'cause of that.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.630
That's why we absolutely
hafta get another player.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:22.090
Ya might be able to convince
Chisato's big sis to join.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.460
We're beggin' ya, Nishina!

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.600
<b>Staff Room</b>

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.300
Excuse me.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.520
<i>Are those two serious?</i>

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.970
<i>I mean, they're right, a cocky
Chiba is a danger to the team,</i>

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:44.300
<i>and the more players we have, the better...</i>

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.030
<b>Art Room</b>

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:50.830
<i>But I don't like the idea of taking
advantage of someone's feelings.</i>

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:52.560
Excuse me.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:53.420
Y-Yes?

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.190
Do you need something from the art club?

00:03:56.190 --> 00:04:01.650
Oh, uh, actually... I was hoping
I could talk to Fujii who's in the art club.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:02.380
Fujii-san?

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:08.150
Oh, as a matter of fact, she just handed me
the paperwork to transfer to another club.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:09.850
She said she was quitting the art club

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.190
so she could join the baseball team.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:18.260
My name is Fujii Chiyo. I'm going
to be the baseball team's new manager.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:19.780
I look forward to working with you.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.740
What?!

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.350
R-Really?

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.240
Yes.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.200
I watched your practice sessions from afar
the past few days and made up my mind.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:33.460
Seeing you all training so hard, I wondered
if I could help you out in some way.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.820
What's goin' on here?

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:37.880
Maybe Nishina missed her?

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:43.400
Ah, well, there's so much to do, we'd be
very grateful to have you as our manager...

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.840
But how about joining as a player?

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.520
I'm afraid I'll have to decline that offer.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:53.250
Like I said before, I really don't think 
I'm athletic enough to play baseball.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.770
What? Seriously?

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:00.190
Are you really joining the baseball team?

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:03.650
Ah, so anyway, I'll go change now.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.030
Yup, but she's joinin' as our manager.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:11.620
I didn't expect her to join
without any prompting.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:14.970
She's <i>seriously</i> got her 
sights set on ya, Nishina.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.290
<i>So I've joined.</i>

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.550
<i>Even though I thought I'd never
get involved with baseball again.</i>

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:27.680
<i>Even though I've been avoiding it since then.</i>

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:31.640
<i>I was never all that
interested in boys, either.</i>

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:34.270
<i>And now I'm here for a younger boy!</i>

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:38.600
Fuurin! Fight! Fight!

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.490
Good work, everyone!

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.870
I'm exhausted.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.770
It's your first day.
It must've been tough to keep up.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:02.540
Well, for you, that was a good effort, Chiyo.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:06.340
Having a manager really makes a difference.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:12.090
With you helping us, everybody's 
training was a lot more effective.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.440
Thank you.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:17.770
<i>I'm sorry, Captain. I'm only here 
because of my impure thoughts.</i>

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:22.000
Your next task is to tidy up 
the field with the first-years.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.430
<i>There's more?!</i>

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:30.620
I'm still wondering why she suddenly 
wanted to become our manager.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:34.050
I mean, Chisato probably
talked her into it, right?

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.030
Hey, everyone.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.710
I wanted to talk to you all
while you're washing up.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.630
We have a practice game
lined up this weekend

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.260
against Tsujidou Middle,
a powerhouse from the region's south.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.170
I'm glad we've got enough people to play.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.580
Huh? We're going up against a team that strong?

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.520
The mushroom only just joined.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.730
Isn't it too early?

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:54.130
But I wanna see what Chiba-kun can do.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:57.570
I have to decide between him
and Tao for the position.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:00.940
I'm thinking of starting 
Chiba-kun at shortstop.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.570
Fujii

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.570
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.180
<i>I need sleep.</i>

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:10.220
<i>I haven't worked myself this hard in a while.</i>

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.740
Chiyo!

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:13.310
Dad?

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:14.790
I heard the news!

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.830
You joined the baseball team!

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.410
What's got into you?

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.400
Oh, but you've made me one happy father!

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:26.340
I thought you hated baseball after
quitting so suddenly back in grade school.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.380
I mean, I'm just the mana—

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.130
Good luck!

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.190
Fuurin is crazy short on players,

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:35.100
so if you work hard, you'll all
get the chance to play in games!

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:39.270
Listen to Daigo and enjoy
your youth to the fullest!

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.560
No, Dad, I'm saying I am—

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.560
All right!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.100
Tonight, I'm breaking out the booze!

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.720
It's time to celebrate!

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:56.880
Chisato, this is all <i>your</i> doing, isn't it?!

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:00.410
You didn't even tell Dad that I'm the manager!

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.830
Hm? Is that what you wanted me to do?

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:08.340
If I'd told him you'd joined the team as
our manager to chase a boy you like,

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.880
he probably would've died of shock.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.130
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.870
I'm not like that!

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.050
I don't even know him!

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.560
Oh, but it's <i>so</i> obvious, Sis.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:20.660
It's Nishina, right?

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.480
You lurve Nishina, don't you?

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:23.960
Shut up!

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.700
You don't know the first thing about me!

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.860
Why do you always make that smug
"I did something!" expression?!

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:32.400
I really <i>hate</i> that about you!

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:37.760
"I did something!" expression? I don't get it.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.030
Is there a smug "I didn't do
something!" expression, too?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.440
Just get out!

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:47.280
What?

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.000
Chiba-kun went home?

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:49.940
Yeah.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:53.330
He said his stomach was hurting, 
so he went home when the bell rang.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.520
I hope he's okay.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:59.970
I hope he doesn't have a cold.
The game's in two days.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:02.600
Maybe he ate some poisonous mushrooms.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.180
That's cannibalism.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.530
He's fakin' it, for sure.

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:11.410
He knew we'd be doin' weights indoors
'cause of the rain, so that moron split.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.720
Yup, probably.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.150
He was late for practice this morning, too.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:19.730
See, Daigo? He's taking more and more
liberties because you're so soft on him!

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:22.640
I mean, we don't have any
proof that he's faking it.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:25.000
I'll get in touch with him
later because I'm worried.

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:27.290
Good job, everyone.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:31.810
Huh? Where're Daigo and the others?

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.560
They already left.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.450
The mushroom wasn't picking up his phone,

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.280
so they went over to his house.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:41.780
Yikes, that means he faked it for sure.

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:44.930
I think even Saint Daigo
can't let this one slide.

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:49.530
Daigo wanted to try the 
mushroom out in the practice game.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:55.110
But in my opinion, it's pointless
until he fixes his attitude.

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:59.050
I'm also ticked off about him 
pitting you two against each other.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:05.180
What's this, Yayoi? Are you worried for me?

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:11.210
Don't worry. There's <i>no way</i> that guy's
taking shortstop away from me!

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:17.670
Vice captain, I have covered
the infield with the tarpaulin.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.970
Right. Thanks.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.860
And you don't have to be 
so formal. We're the same age.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:25.140
As for calling me "vice captain"...

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.000
Oh, right.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:29.920
But I was really surprised.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:30.900
Excuse me?

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:33.860
You pretty much kept up
with our training regimen.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.570
So you must be fit after all.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:41.370
Well, I did tennis and swimming 
back in grade school, so...

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:45.110
You said you were unathletic before,
but is that really true?

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:48.100
From the way you move,
I really don't get that impression.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:54.420
I heard you played baseball with your 
father and sister back in grade school.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:58.300
And according to Chisato, 
you're not unathletic at all.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:01.510
She said she didn't know 
why you quit baseball.

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:02.910
So why did you?

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:07.470
<i>Yes?</i>

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:12.670
Oh, hello, we're on the
Fuurin Middle baseball team.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.390
We wondered if Chiba-kun was in.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:15.450
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:17.480
<i>Oh, you're my brother's teammates?</i>

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:18.990
<i>Takumi's in the hospital.</i>

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:19.810
What?

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:21.710
Th-The hospital?

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:26.330
<i>I just heard back from him. Apparently,
they're keeping him there for a week.</i>

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.460
Appendicitis?!

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:41.170
Which means Chiba-kun won't
be playing in our next game.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.330
So what're we gonna do now?

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:45.140
We can't field enough players.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:48.510
Well, there is <i>one</i> way we can solve that.

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:52.130
What?

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:54.270
N-No, it's not happening!

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:55.730
I'm begging you!

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:57.860
You can be in the outfield. Just please play!

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.190
B-But...

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.710
Practice games are so important!

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:05.440
If we don't play this one,
who knows when our next one will be!

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:07.280
Please, Chiyo!

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:09.310
Yeah, but...

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.810
Ya can jus' stand there!

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:13.150
Please!

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:15.850
Hey now, aren't you going a bit overboard?

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:17.610
Ya oughta ask her too!

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:18.030
Huh?

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:19.630
Yeah, come on!

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.510
You want my sister to play, right?

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:24.720
Huh? I... Well, I...

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:32.560
<b>Fuu</b>

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:37.020
How did this happen?

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:40.610
Am I really going to play in the game?

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:44.200
<b>Fuu</b>

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.490
You want my sister to play, right?

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:46.750
Huh? I... Well, I...

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:51.000
I mean, you already joined the club, right?

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.250
It'd be great if you did just
 a <i>touch</i> more and gave it a shot.

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.590
<b>Fuu</b>

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:09.270
<i>I don't want to be a burden on everyone.</i>

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:12.310
<i>I don't want him to be disappointed!</i>

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:15.310
Just a touch. A tiny chunk. Chiyo.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.440
Hey, Sis.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:28.870
How long are you gonna stay
on there? They're for babies!

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:31.950
Let's play catch! Come on, let's play!

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:35.680
But I wanted to play on the swing...

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:40.840
Oh, come on, this is much better!
It's baseball! Let's play baseball!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:46.300
Dad said I should get you to
teach me when he's at work.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:50.850
I want to get good like you, Sis!

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:55.520
If I get good, I can start training with
the Dolphins when I get to third grade!

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:00.940
Here we go!

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:02.950
I-Isn't this too close?

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.730
It's fine, it's fine!

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:06.150
I'm younger than you.

00:14:20.410 --> 00:14:24.540
<i>I think I just had a really awful dream.</i>

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.370
Are you all right, Chiyo?

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:30.100
Oh, I'm fine.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:33.640
Were you still sleeping?
You need to hurry up and get ready.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.330
It's our practice game 
with that other school today.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:41.690
<b>Fuu</b>

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:41.690
<b>rin</b>

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:40.640
I ain't heard of this Tsujidou.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:41.690
Are they good?

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:45.820
They're a new private school
that opened three years ago,

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.050
so they haven't achieved a lot yet,

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:50.870
but it looks like they've
gotten really strong lately.

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:53.540
Especially in the last fall tournament.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:58.140
They went all the way to
regionals and placed second.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:01.800
Playing a team like that doesn't make sense.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.430
Why didn't you just say no?

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:05.310
The mushroom's in hospital.

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:09.510
And we're fieldin' our green manager
jus' to make this game happen?

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.590
We're gonna lose so hard!

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:19.140
Well, I asked all the major names to
play us because it'd be an education,

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:21.310
but none of them said yes.

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:24.590
Then, out of the blue, this school agreed.

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.420
It would've been a waste to cancel.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:27.780
That's all ya can say?

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:32.260
I am a little worried about
putting Chiyo out in left field,

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:34.160
but judging from yesterday's practice,

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:39.330
her experience at junior level means
she can handle simple fly balls.

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:44.880
W-Well, let's just use this opportunity to
check out one of the top teams in our region.

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:48.480
We should just aim at preventing 
the game being called.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:51.350
This ain't funny.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:54.660
That mushroom's freakin' useless.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:58.890
How are you feeling after the op?

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:00.950
I feel really good. Great, even.

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:03.860
That jello dessert was pretty good.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:06.020
Oh, and could I get a coke or something?

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:06.860
Not happening!

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:10.820
This school's pretty fancy, ain't it?

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:15.160
It's brand-new, and it's a prep school for
the adjoining high school, just like ours.

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:18.750
A field just for the baseball team!

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:19.690
It's huge!

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:22.110
They're playing a game.

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:25.530
It's not intra-team, either.
That's a different school's uniform.

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:27.090
Look.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:35.180
North Sayama

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:35.180
North Sayama

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:35.180
Tsujidou

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:35.180
Tsujidou

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:31.140
Seems like a pretty good contest.

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:32.650
North Sayama?

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:35.180
Ain't Sayama a Saitama school?!

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:39.540
So they came all the way from 
Saitama to play this team?

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:42.770
I guess they've gotten strong enough
for others to want to play them.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.150
Oh, there you are!

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:46.560
Hi.

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.480
Oh, Yamaguchi-sensei.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:49.860
She's here too, huh?

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:52.720
Thank you for coming on your day off.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.660
You could've skipped this one, you know.

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:59.160
The adviser has to accompany
the team to practice games.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.580
It's one of the rules.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.440
This game will be over soon.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:08.420
They said we should warm up out here
somewhere until our game starts at 11.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.670
All right.

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:14.380
Oh, and they have a special rule in place.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:15.340
Huh?

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:17.150
A special rule?

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:22.810
It looks like each team gets an assigned 
handicap based on their strength.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:23.980
A handicap?

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:30.940
North Sayama

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:30.940
North Sayama

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:30.940
Tsujidou

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:30.940
Tsujidou

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:29.510
North Sayama were given those five
runs in the first inning as a handicap.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:36.530
Y-You say it depends on the team's strength? 
So how many runs will we start with?

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:41.370
Not sure. They said they'd write it
on the scoreboard at the start of the game.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.270
Bow!

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.000
Let's have a good game!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:51.210
Fuurin

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:51.210
Fuurin

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:51.210
Tsujidou

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:51.210
Tsujidou

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:50.860
I didn't expect them to
treat us like total losers.

00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:53.550
We <i>really</i> need to show them now!

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.600
Let's do this!

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:59.720
<i>Batting first, center field,
Fujii Chisato-san.</i>

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:04.070
This is how they treat their
guests? It's freakin' rude.

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:07.110
Aren't they being nice?

00:18:07.110 --> 00:18:10.950
We're guests and we have a lot of girls, 
so they're giving us this on the house.

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:13.520
Oh, so this is like Ladies' Night?

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:15.320
Must be nice bein' that dense.

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:21.590
<i>So they think they can beat us even
when we start with a ten-run lead?</i>

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:23.950
Play ball!

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:27.040
<i>We'll make them regret doing that.</i>

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:31.380
<i>Not only will we stop them winning,
we'll beat them by eleven runs!</i>

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.450
Strike! You're out!

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:40.450
Three outs!

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:41.220
Change sides!

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:42.550
H-Huh?

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.920
A-All right! We're ten runs ahead!

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:47.560
So we're relyin' on the handicap?

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:50.850
We're switching now, Chiyo.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.520
R-Right.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:53.900
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:57.040
<i>I just hope a ball doesn't come my way.</i>

00:18:57.040 --> 00:19:00.320
<i>This is basically my first real game ever!</i>

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:02.570
Hurry up, will you?

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:06.740
If you're already on two outs,
at least have your shin guards on!

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:07.790
Idiot!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.850
Ah, I-I'm sorry!

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:11.620
<i>I got yelled at.</i>

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:16.280
Must be rough only having nine players.

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:19.670
What's up with this team anyway, Coach?

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:23.570
Not only are they short on players,
with no backup catcher,

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:26.000
but of the nine players they
do have, seven are girls.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:30.410
And looking at their recent record,
they didn't even make it through the prelims.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:36.360
What's the point in playing a team like this?

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:39.500
I'd like to know the answer to that myself.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:42.200
You'll have to ask the head coach, 
who arranged this game.

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:45.320
Maybe the ten-run handicap wasn't enough.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:46.990
<i>Batting first, second base, Tokugawa-kun.</i>

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.370
Fuurin

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.370
Fuurin

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.370
Tsujidou

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.370
Tsujidou

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:50.370
We've got Nishina, so just
cut loose in the first inning.

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:52.480
It'll be fine.

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:56.960
If you throw your regular pitches, they won't
hit them easily, no matter how good they are.

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.550
I'm worried about Anita on first

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:02.510
and Chiyo out in left field,

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:06.220
but in the past six months,
 all of us have improved.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.310
Let's show them Fuurin's Girl Power!

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:14.020
We'll make them sorry for
handing us that ten-run lead!

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:16.230
Strike!

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:19.020
That was a nice throw for a girl.

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:20.690
She's got nice form.

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:24.160
Ball.

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:26.120
Ball.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.700
She might lack control, though.

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:31.910
Strike!

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:37.790
Yeah! A hit!

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:44.050
S-Safe!

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:44.940
Yes!

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:46.120
Nice running!

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:47.780
Tch.

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:49.970
That wasn't out?

00:20:50.380 --> 00:20:51.810
Don't worry about it!

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.880
That shortstop's pretty good.

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:57.150
Even Tokugawa at top speed barely made it.

00:20:57.580 --> 00:21:00.610
<i>Batting second, right field, Takada-kun.</i>

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:02.890
<i>Don't rush.</i>

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:07.490
Safe!

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:09.400
<i>You're doing good, Mutsuko.</i>

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:10.580
<i>Nice and calm.</i>

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.350
Strike!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.080
<i>So that I don't disgrace my ace number,</i>

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:20.160
<i>I've upped my pitching speed
by more than 5 kmph.</i>

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:21.750
<i>Gaining five kilos sucks, though.</i>

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:25.060
<i>We can't fear teams like these...</i>

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:28.960
<i>...if we want to make it to regionals!</i>

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:34.110
All right!

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:39.500
Out!

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:41.800
Nice, Yayoi!

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:43.190
Nice double play!

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:46.400
Yay.

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:48.990
Two outs!

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:54.430
<i>Batting third, catcher, Inoue-kun.</i>

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:01.540
Good job!

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:02.130
This time it's a hit!

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:08.050
Too bad!

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:09.370
Three outs!

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:10.220
What?!

00:22:11.320 --> 00:22:12.840
Nice, Chisato!

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:14.470
Yes!

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:16.430
Fuurin

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:16.430
Fuurin

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:16.430
Tsujidou

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:16.430
Tsujidou

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:16.430
<i>I see.</i>

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:21.650
<i>Looks like playing them 
wasn't a complete mistake.</i>

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:23.070
Good one.

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:24.140
That was amazing.

00:22:24.140 --> 00:22:25.610
<i>Chisato's one thing...</i>

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:29.010
<i>But </i>all<i> of these guys are really good!</i>

00:24:00.270 --> 00:24:01.500
You can do this!

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:03.040
You can hit it, Chiyo!

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:04.340
I-I can't!

00:24:04.340 --> 00:24:07.880
It's too high a level for me. I don't
understand how you can all hit those pitches.

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:11.260
There's a secret method to it.

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:12.880
You can hit them too!

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:15.260
No, I'm not like you, Chisato!

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:17.890
I'm only here to make up the numbers.

00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:20.200
Don't say that!

00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>You Disappoint Me!</b>

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:22.420
Next time: "You Disappoint Me!"

00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:24.670
Run to the stage of your dreams!
